    \field{labelnamesource}{author}
    \field{labeltitlesource}{title}
    \field{sortinit}{B}
    \field{sortinithash}{B}
    \field{abstract}{%
    In this paper we study the computational complexity of the capacitated lot
  size problem with a particular cost structure that is likely to be used in
  practical settings. For the single item case new properties are introduced,
  classes of problems solvable by polynomial time algorithms are identified,
  and efficient solution procedures are given. We show that special classes are
  NP-hard, and that the problem with two items and independent setups is
  NP-hard under conditions similar to those where the single item problem is
  easy. Topics for further research are discussed in the last section.%
    }
