    \strng{namehash}{LZFZKL1}
    \strng{fullhash}{LZFZKL1}
    \field{labelnamesource}{author}
    \field{labeltitlesource}{title}
    \field{sortinit}{L}
    \field{sortinithash}{L}
    \field{abstract}{%
    In this study, fireworks algorithm (FWA) for the multi-satellite control
  resource scheduling problem (MSCRSP) is presented. FWA is a meta-heuristic
  method and widely used in continuous problems while MSCRSP is a constrained
  and large scale combinatorial problem. The key points of FWA are to define a
  suitable neighborhood structure for launching the local search procedure and
  to find a metric for quantifying the disparity between solutions. Three kinds
  of neighborhood structures are presented and the best fitted one is picked.
  Due to the speciality of this problem, each solution is transformed into a
  binary vector, and Hamming distance is adopted for defining disparity metric.
  The experimental results demonstrate the proposed FWA is more competitive
  than those commonly used methods.%
    }
    \field{booktitle}{2015 IEEE Congress on Evolutionary Computation (CEC)}
    \verb{doi}
    \verb 10.1109/CEC.2015.7257036
    \endverb
    \field{pages}{1280\bibrangedash 1286}
    \field{title}{Fireworks algorithm for the multi-satellite control resource
  scheduling problem}
    \field{year}{2015}
    \warn{\item Invalid format of field 'month'}
  \endentry

